#+TITLE: Host CL compiler diagnostics leak on stdout/stderr
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: bug
#+BRANCH: fix-host-compiler-diagnostics-leak

Host CL compiler diagnostics leak on stdout/stderr

== Symptom ==

Running an AutoLISP program prints Common Lisp compiler chatter the user
never asked for: SBCL/CCL style warnings, optimization notes and progress
lines about *generated* Common Lisp they did not write. It surfaces during
ordinary execution, not only when compiling an artefact.

== Cause ==

The AutoLISP→CL compiler (compiler.issue) hands transpiled bodies to the host
Common Lisp compiler:

- lazily, when a function crosses *AUTOLISP-COMPILATION-THRESHOLD* — so it
  fires mid-run, on the call that made a function hot;
- eagerly at SPEED 3 (the LOAD is wrapped in one WITH-COMPILATION-UNIT);
- and when CLAL-COMPILE-FILE writes a .lap artefact.

Each of those calls (compile-usubr / compile-instrumented-usubr /
compile-autolisp-form / compile-file, and the runtime's eager
WITH-COMPILATION-UNIT) let the host compiler narrate on *error-output*.
COMPILE-FILE already passed :VERBOSE NIL :PRINT NIL, but that only stops the
progress lines, not the style warnings and notes.

== Fix (clautolisp 2.2.82) ==

New runtime facility (autolisp-runtime):

- ~*emit-host-compiler-diagnostics*~ — NIL by default (muffle).
- ~with-muffled-host-compiler~ / ~call-with-muffled-host-compiler~ — bind
  *COMPILE-VERBOSE* / *COMPILE-PRINT* NIL and muffle WARNING (covers style
  warnings and CCL compiler-warnings) and, on SBCL, SB-EXT:COMPILER-NOTE.
  Errors are NOT muffled — a real compilation failure still signals, so the
  callers' :FAILED handling and COMPILE-FILE's FAILUREP are unaffected.

Every host compile site is wrapped: the runtime's eager WITH-COMPILATION-UNIT
and the compiler's compile-usubr / compile-instrumented-usubr /
compile-autolisp-form / compile-autolisp-files-to-lap.

The clautolisp CLI raises ~*emit-host-compiler-diagnostics*~ to T under
--verbose / --debug (main.lisp, the run-time LET around RUN-WITH-INPUT), for
someone debugging the compiler itself.

== Resolved ==

DONE — clautolisp 2.2.82 (2026-09-23). Tests in
autolisp-runtime/tests/evaluator-tests.lisp (the
with-muffled-host-compiler-* group, incl. an SBCL compile-note case);
runtime suite 950/950 and compiler suite 396/396 green. Documented in the
clautolisp user manual (--verbose / --debug) and RELEASE_NOTES.org.
